      "description": "Watch LA Galaxy vs San Jose Earthquakes highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The California rivalry intensified on August 20, 2026, as LA Galaxy hosted San Jose Earthquakes in a MLS clash defined by tactical discipline and a crucial disciplinary shift. Both sides entered the pitch looking to claim dominance in a match where every challenge felt significant from the opening whistle. Disciplinary Drama and the Red Card The first half was a feisty affair, with the referee's notebook filling up early. Harbor Miller saw yellow for the hosts in the 24th minute, while San Jose 's Nick Fernandez and Lucas Sanabria were also cautioned. The game's complexion changed entirely just before the interval when Sanabria committed a second bookable offense. His dismissal in the 45th minute left the Earthquakes a man down, handing LA Galaxy a massive psychological and tactical advantage heading into the break. Paintsil Delivers the Decisive Blow Utilizing their numerical superiority in the second half, LA Galaxy began to pin the visitors back. Despite tactical adjustments from San Jose , including the introduction of Timo Werner and Ousseni Bouda , the pressure eventually became overwhelming. In the 79th minute, the breakthrough finally arrived. Harbor Miller turned provider, setting up Joseph Paintsil , who finished clinicaly to break the deadlock. Although the Earthquakes fought bravely to the end, receiving further cautions through Jack Jasinski and Justin Haak , the Galaxy managed the closing stages professionally to secure a hard-fought victory."
